WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.500
Samaya Sterling beats Claude Fable 5.1 on Frontier Finance at 111th the cost. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 219. Based in Joey 1, Mistral's public large 4, and ARC transcriber follow, then things to try. Samaya AI has Sterling out as a low rank adaptation, or Laura, post train of NVIDIA's Nemotron 3.5 Lightning, according to Mark Tech Post. The base is a 30 billion parameter mixture of experts, or MOE,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.760
model with 3 billion parameters active, aimed at agentic financial research.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.940
Sterling lays out a research plan, invokes 37 finance tools, collects evidence, and passes

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.820
the packet to a separate report writer.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:51.760
It scores 58.9% on frontier finance, and 60.6% in high effort mode, against 55.9% for

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.320
Claude Fable 5.1.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:59.000
The bill is $0.61 per question against $6.89 for the larger model.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:05.120
Training ran four Laura stages on synthetic traces from Kemi-K3, with condenser and

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.420
compactor helpers to hold context down.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:15.720
The base fits a single H-180 gigabyte card in BF-16 at 256,000 context, and Sterling adds

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.740
a research budget cap that stops the agent before the report writer takes over.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:26.297
However, production classifiers can skip generative calls with Joey 1, a 2-billion-parameter open-weight

00:01:26.297 --> 00:01:30.137
decision model that returns calibrated probabilities instead of text.

00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:34.637
It runs at 20 milliseconds at the 50th percentile on standard hardware.

00:01:35.177 --> 00:01:37.657
The price is 1 cent per million input tokens.

00:01:38.177 --> 00:01:43.517
The target is classification and regression when labeled data already exists, and a freeform

00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:45.137
generate would be wasted spend.

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:49.897
And based on puts it in production pipelines that need a probability, not a paragraph.

00:01:50.946 --> 00:01:56.466
Meastral AI released large four publicly, Reuters said, with an explicit focus on cyber

00:01:56.466 --> 00:01:57.446
security workloads.

00:01:57.866 --> 00:02:01.586
The model is aimed at detection and analysis tasks in that domain.

00:02:02.286 --> 00:02:07.986
Arc transcriber folds automatic speech recognition, or ASR, together with named entity linking,

00:02:08.306 --> 00:02:13.466
number extraction, speaker segmentation, and dialogue act tagging, a machine learning

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.226
thread reports.

00:02:14.226 --> 00:02:19.546
The whole stack is approximately 70 megabytes, streams, and uses no second model.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.846
A single forward pass lands every 100 milliseconds.

00:02:23.426 --> 00:02:28.986
Two variants ship, ARC Mini on a moonshot encoder and ARC V1 on a parakeeting coder.

00:02:29.426 --> 00:02:34.866
Wates in a command line interface, or CLI, sit on hugging face and GitHub for on-device use.

00:02:35.366 --> 00:02:40.246
The model carries over 200 trained decision heads and can prime itself with a user-supplied

00:02:40.246 --> 00:02:43.866
roster of names or titles for live-fact checking inside the stream.

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:51.034
OpenAI now monitors all frontier reinforcement learning, or RL, runs, evaluations, and

00:02:51.034 --> 00:02:52.294
internal codex use.

00:02:52.874 --> 00:02:57.254
The stack uses activation probes, reviewer models, and investigative agents.

00:02:57.774 --> 00:03:02.854
It caught a September domain name system, or DNS, misconfiguration breach in 15 minutes.

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:08.554
It also replayed the earlier hugging face incident and alerted responders 30 minutes after escape.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:13.094
human responders get rapid alerts when behavior leaves the intended boundaries.

00:03:14.112 --> 00:03:18.192
Anthropic added self-assessment so Claude scores its own conversation for

00:03:18.192 --> 00:03:22.552
misuse right after it replies. The check has surface misuse that prior

00:03:22.552 --> 00:03:27.012
classifiers missed since June. It improves as the underlying model improves.

00:03:27.532 --> 00:03:31.512
Because the model has already read the full conversation, the past runs without a

00:03:31.512 --> 00:03:36.948
separate classifier. Late in space is running the invite-only AIE code summit for

00:03:36.948 --> 00:03:39.148
the top 1,000-agentic engineers.

00:03:39.668 --> 00:03:44.768
The focus is scaling without junk output, system-1 decision models, and ambitious rewrites

00:03:44.768 --> 00:03:46.468
of browsers and design suites.

00:03:47.008 --> 00:03:52.288
The single-track event previews 2027 themes after last year's skills and software factories

00:03:52.288 --> 00:03:52.688
tracks.

00:03:53.368 --> 00:03:58.828
Jard Sumner will discuss bun ahead of time, or AOT, compilation, and new compiler features

00:03:58.828 --> 00:04:00.128
tried with a small team.

00:04:01.169 --> 00:04:07.049
TK Integers puts balance-turnary K5 weights in one bite per code, a machine learning thread

00:04:07.049 --> 00:04:12.509
reports and runs them on existing FP-16 tensor cores with no native K5 instructions.

00:04:13.229 --> 00:04:21.569
On Quen 2.5-0.5 B-instruct, the kernels delivered 3.2-1 times pre-fill and 3.10 times decode

00:04:21.569 --> 00:04:25.829
throughput versus torch AOFP8 on an NVIDIA L4 GPU.

00:04:26.529 --> 00:04:30.089
The repo ships a converter, native kernels, and benchmark scripts.

00:04:30.649 --> 00:04:35.109
Some tensors stay in higher precision while bounded tiles expand for tensor core math.

00:04:35.109 --> 00:04:41.056
Paired per question outcomes, not just a headline score, are what one thread demanded when

00:04:41.056 --> 00:04:46.696
an MOE back end, an FP8 output head, and speculative decoding all change at once.

00:04:47.356 --> 00:04:54.896
The poster showed two GSM 8K runs that differ by 0.07 points across 1,319 questions.

00:04:55.356 --> 00:04:59.256
The ask is paired per question outcomes or a declared equivalence margin.

00:04:59.836 --> 00:05:04.656
The fight is whether aggregate scores alone can carry a quality neutral claim when several

00:05:04.656 --> 00:05:12.156
optimization's ship together. Two more briefs, Casup raised $56 million to expand its AI agent

00:05:12.156 --> 00:05:18.116
platform for financial services workflows. AI Insider reports, Nature published a clinical

00:05:18.116 --> 00:05:23.896
