00:05:57.769 --> 00:06:02.909
Additional institutions are in line for anthropic AI for science credits as the program expands

00:06:02.909 --> 00:06:07.729
beyond individual researchers. Further open-weight decision and streaming models

00:06:07.729 --> 00:06:12.709
are likely as teams copy the small act of parameter recipe. More cyber security

00:06:12.709 --> 00:06:18.337
capability detail on Meastraw-Large 4 is expected after the public release. One

00:06:18.337 --> 00:06:22.897
extra forward pass per decision is the tax if we pop the hood on sequential Bayesian

00:06:22.897 --> 00:06:28.117
experimental design for verification tasks. Sequential Bayesian experimental design

00:06:28.117 --> 00:06:33.297
treats the next verification query as an optimization. Maximize expected information

00:06:33.297 --> 00:06:38.697
gain per unit cost rather than just shrinking uncertainty. The loop stores a posterior

00:06:38.697 --> 00:06:43.737
over the quantity being measured. It then chooses the query whose outcome distribution cuts

00:06:43.737 --> 00:06:49.857
posterior entropy the most after subtracting that query's expected cost. When geographic or

00:06:49.857 --> 00:06:55.177
incentive bias sits in the verifier pool, importance weights or stratified sampling go inside

00:06:55.177 --> 00:07:00.077
that same objective. So the pick tasks fix coverage without a separate cleanup pass.

00:07:00.577 --> 00:07:04.237
A regression approximates the value function during backward induction,

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:09.137
which lets the policy improve on every new batch of outcomes instead of locking a fixed

00:07:09.137 --> 00:07:14.277
open loop schedule. One formulation casts the whole sequence as a dynamic program,

00:07:14.717 --> 00:07:19.077
and its special cases recover both batch design and myopic greedy selection.

00:07:19.777 --> 00:07:24.857
Numerical runs on three different examples beat baselines that ignore cost or sample efficiency.

00:07:25.177 --> 00:07:31.157
After a few hundred labeled examples, the policy cuts total verification spend by 30-40%

00:07:31.157 --> 00:07:32.977
on crowdsource labeling tasks.

00:07:33.457 --> 00:07:38.117
The method fits when the verification budget is the binding constraint and labeled outcomes

00:07:38.117 --> 00:07:41.037
arrive slowly enough to support those regression updates.

00:07:41.777 --> 00:07:46.977
Poorly calibrated cost estimates make the policy oversample cheap, low information tasks.

